# Build output, and bytes this repository did not write.
**/dist/
release/
node_modules/

# The engine CI checks out at the workspace root so the live tests have something to spawn
# (RG111) — a whole repository of them, and Prettier walks from the root exactly as oxlint
# does. Ignored by git too; this says it again where the gate reads.
/roadkeep/

# Captured engine and session output, kept exactly as a real run printed it. Reformatting
# it would make the fixture a formatter's idea of what the engine says.
packages/shell/src/captured/

# roadkeep writes these: `roadkeep install` rewrites them from its own checkout and reports
# a stale one against it. Formatting them makes every copy differ from the source it came
# from, so the gate says the surfaces are behind when only a formatter has been past.
.claude/skills/roadkeep/

# The design system writes these, for the same reason and with the same consequence:
# `viglet-ds-page-reference` rewrites them from the package and reports a difference as
# drift, so a formatter passing over one turns the gate red against nothing.
.claude/skills/viglet-ds-pages/

# The source of a published design canvas, and a formatter would rewrite it into something
# that canvas never published — the two ends would stop round-tripping. One artboard is the
# harder case: it shows a governed section with the wrapping the file stores, inside a
# `white-space: pre-wrap` block, so reindenting it changes what the drawing demonstrates.
docs/design/*.dc.html

# roadkeep owns these five and refuses a hand edit; a formatter is a hand edit.
docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/CHANGELOG.md
docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md
docs/DECISIONS.md
docs/DEFERRED.md
